From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000032 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac <steamac@localhost>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 20:20:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 32/32] MSL: Reserve log10 for the Metal standard library

STEAMAC-1R: the compute shader defines an ACES spline helper named log10,
emitted as float log10(thread const float&). Metal also imports
metal::log10(float) via using namespace metal; a float lvalue matches both,
so the call is ambiguous. This is not an integer/half conversion problem.

Add log10 to the existing MSL illegal-function-name set so definitions and
calls receive the same normal rename. GLSL's reserved list covers log/log2,
but not this Metal-only name. Keep the user helper's implementation.
---

diff --git a/spirv_msl.cpp b/spirv_msl.cpp
--- a/spirv_msl.cpp
+++ b/spirv_msl.cpp
@@ -18914,6 +18914,7 @@
 		"fragment",
 		"vertex",
 		"kernel",
+		"log10",
 		"saturate",
 		"assert",
 		"fmin3",
